# Chiral flux phase in the Kagome superconductor AV3Sb5

## Key equations (hand-transcribed)

NN kagome tight-binding (Eq. 1):
$$H_k=\begin{pmatrix} -\mu & -2t\cos(k_1/2) & -2t\cos(k_2/2)\\ -2t\cos(k_1/2) & -\mu & -2t\cos(k_3/2)\\ -2t\cos(k_2/2) & -2t\cos(k_3/2) & -\mu \end{pmatrix}$$
with $k_1=k_x,\; k_2=\tfrac12 k_x+\tfrac{\sqrt3}{2}k_y,\; k_3=-\tfrac12 k_x+\tfrac{\sqrt3}{2}k_y$.

vCDW order (Eq. 4): $\Delta_{vCDW}(R)=\lambda(\cos Q_a\!\cdot\!R,\cos Q_b\!\cdot\!R,\cos Q_c\!\cdot\!R)$
CBO order (Eq. 7): $\Delta_{CBO}(R)=\lambda(\cos Q_a\!\cdot\!R,\cos Q_b\!\cdot\!R,\cos Q_c\!\cdot\!R)$ (real bond)
CFP order (Eq. 9): $\Delta_{CFP}(R)=i\lambda(\cos Q_a\!\cdot\!R,\cos Q_b\!\cdot\!R,\cos Q_c\!\cdot\!R)$ (imaginary bond = loop current)
Kubo Hall (Eq. 10): $\sigma_{xy}=\frac{e^2}{\hbar}\sum_{k,n,m}\frac{[f(\epsilon_{nk})-f(\epsilon_{mk})]\,\mathrm{Im}(v_x^{nm}v_y^{mn})}{(\epsilon_{nk}-\epsilon_{mk})^2}$

Headline: at $\lambda=0.3$, $E_{CFP}$ is $0.195t$ below CBO and $0.435t$ below vCDW per unit cell; occupied CFP bands give $C=1$/spin, $\sigma_{xy}=2e^2/h$.

